<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>FIELD — an instrument for looking closer</title><meta name="description" content="An open-source cinematic study of light, focus and perspective.">
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 64 64'%3E%3Ccircle cx='32' cy='32' r='29' fill='%238F6A38'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='32' cy='32' r='16' fill='none' stroke='%23E9E1D4'/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./story.css"></head>
<body class="field-story"><a class="skip" href="#story">Skip to the story</a>
<header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href="#">FIELD <em>instruments</em></a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="#observe">The instrument</a><a href="#make">Make it yours</a></nav><a class="source" href="../effects-lab/">Effects lab ↗</a></header>
<main id="story">
  <section class="field-intro"><p class="eyebrow">An open study / No. 001</p><h1>There is more<br> to <em>looking.</em></h1><div class="field-intro-foot"><p>Open the iris to discover the contours within.<br> Scroll to change your point of view.</p><a href="#observe" class="button">Look a little closer ↓</a></div><span class="field-index" aria-hidden="true">01 — ∞</span></section>
  <section id="observe" class="observatory" aria-label="Explore light, focus and perspective">
    <div class="instrument-shell">
      <div class="instrument">
        <svg class="field-optics" viewBox="0 0 600 600" role="img" aria-labelledby="optics-title optics-desc">
          <title id="optics-title">An iris opening onto a contour landscape</title>
          <desc id="optics-desc">Six graphite blades frame fine brass contour lines. Opening the aperture reveals more of the same landscape.</desc>
          <defs>
            <radialGradient id="terrain-light"><stop stop-color="#C6AD82"/><stop offset=".55" stop-color="#71644F"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#252A2B"/></radialGradient>
            <linearGradient id="blade-light" x2="1" y2="1"><stop stop-color="#444A4B"/><stop offset=".55" stop-color="#252B2D"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#14191B"/></linearGradient>
            <clipPath id="field-window"><circle cx="300" cy="300" r="242"/></clipPath>
            <mask id="iris-mask"><rect width="600" height="600" fill="white"/><circle id="iris-opening" cx="300" cy="300" r="142" fill="black"/></mask>
          </defs>
          <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="282" fill="#151A1C" stroke="#6B6D65" stroke-width="1"/>
          <g clip-path="url(#field-window)">
            <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="245" fill="url(#terrain-light)"/>
            <g class="terrain-contours" fill="none" stroke="#E1D3B9" stroke-width="1.2"><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="70" ry="32" transform="rotate(-28 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="87" ry="44" transform="rotate(-26 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="104" ry="56" transform="rotate(-24 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="121" ry="68" transform="rotate(-22 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="138" ry="80" transform="rotate(-20 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="155" ry="92" transform="rotate(-18 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="172" ry="104" transform="rotate(-16 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="189" ry="116" transform="rotate(-14 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="206" ry="128" transform="rotate(-12 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="223" ry="140" transform="rotate(-10 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="240" ry="152" transform="rotate(-8 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="257" ry="164" transform="rotate(-6 310 300)"/><ellipse cx="310" cy="300" rx="274" ry="176" transform="rotate(-4 310 300)"/><path d="M120 440Q220 250 330 270T530 150M95 390Q210 205 320 220T500 120" stroke-width="2"/></g>
            <g mask="url(#iris-mask)"><circle cx="300" cy="300" r="245" fill="#202629"/><g class="iris-blades" fill="url(#blade-light)" stroke="#6A6C64" stroke-width="1"><path d="M300 300L300 30Q485 25 548 155L410 350Z" transform="rotate(0 300 300)"/><path d="M300 300L300 30Q485 25 548 155L410 350Z" transform="rotate(60 300 300)"/><path d="M300 300L300 30Q485 25 548 155L410 350Z" transform="rotate(120 300 300)"/><path d="M300 300L300 30Q485 25 548 155L410 350Z" transform="rotate(180 300 300)"/><path d="M300 300L300 30Q485 25 548 155L410 350Z" transform="rotate(240 300 300)"/><path d="M300 300L300 30Q485 25 548 155L410 350Z" transform="rotate(300 300 300)"/></g></g>
            <circle id="iris-edge" cx="300" cy="300" r="142" fill="none" stroke="#C7AB7C" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          </g>
          <g fill="none" stroke="#918574"><circle cx="300" cy="300" r="258" stroke-width=".5"/><circle cx="300" cy="300" r="268" stroke-width="7" stroke-dasharray="1 13"/><path d="M300 12v31m0 514v31M12 300h31m514 0h31" stroke-width="1"/></g>
          <g fill="#CFC5B4" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="10" letter-spacing="3" text-anchor="middle"><text x="300" y="73">FIELD / 001</text><text x="300" y="535">AN EXERCISE IN ATTENTION</text></g>
        </svg>
        <span class="instrument-mark mark-n" aria-hidden="true">OPTICAL STUDY</span>
      </div>
      <div class="field-controls" hidden><label for="focus">Aperture <input id="focus" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="45"><output for="focus" id="focus-value">45%</output></label><button type="button" id="field-reset">Reset</button><button type="button" id="field-pause" aria-pressed="false">Pause motion</button></div>
      <noscript><p class="field-hint">The iris is shown at 45% open. Enable JavaScript to adjust its opening.</p></noscript>
      <p class="field-hint">One landscape, a changing frame. Open the aperture to reveal the outer contours.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field-beats">
      <article class="field-beat"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Observe</p><h2>Start with<br> a <em>detail.</em></h2><p>The narrow opening isolates a few contours. Before you see the whole landscape, follow the lines that pass through its centre.</p><span class="beat-note">A small frame concentrates your attention.</span></article>
      <article class="field-beat"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Focus</p><h2>Let the<br> world <em>in.</em></h2><p>Open the aperture and watch the six blades withdraw. More of the same terrain appears: a detail becomes part of a larger pattern.</p><span class="beat-note">Try the aperture at both ends of its range.</span></article>
      <article class="field-beat"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Reframe</p><h2>Same place.<br> New <em>perspective.</em></h2><p>As you move down the page, the contours turn within their frame. Return to the beginning to see the same landscape from your first viewpoint.</p><span class="beat-note">Reverse your scroll to retrace the view.</span></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="field-principles"><div><p class="eyebrow">Inside the study</p><h2>A landscape.<br> Six blades.<br> <em>Your attention.</em></h2></div><div class="principle-list"><article><span>01</span><h3>The landscape stays</h3><p>The contours are drawn once. Opening the iris reveals their surroundings rather than replacing the subject.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>The frame changes</h3><p>The aperture sets the opening; scrolling changes the viewpoint. Pause the motion and explore the iris at your own pace.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>The idea is yours to adapt</h3><p>This is an imagined instrument, not a simulation of lens physics. Its source is available under MIT for your own experiments.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="closing" id="make"><p class="eyebrow">Your perspective is the missing ingredient.</p><h2>What will you<br> <em>bring into focus?</em></h2><a class="button" href="https://github.com/MustBeSimo/cinematic-scroll-skill">Make something of your own ↗</a></section>
</main><footer><a class="wordmark" href="#">FIELD <em>instruments</em></a><p>A fictional instrument. A working open-source study.</p><a href="../effects-lab/">Explore the ingredients ↗</a></footer>
